# Why templates need their own temporary IR

Look at the page fragment again:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
[$html:
    <p>[greet(visitor)]</p>
]
]

A template is not a string with holes poked by hope. It contains structure: wrappers, slots, child values, control flow and placement order. Flatten it too early and you lose the skeleton the checker and the runtime both need.

Moth gives templates a first-class home and a temporary **Template IR (TIR)** that lives only while AST work runs.

## Template structure

The fragment wants a paragraph wrapper, an interpolation of a string-producing call and a stable place in the page's fragment order.

If the compiler treated the body as blind concatenation, it could still emit characters on a happy path. It would struggle to:

- type-check slot contents
- fold pure pieces while keeping dynamic pieces honest
- preserve source locations for diagnostics
- attach constrained reactivity metadata
- hand a neutral runtime plan to HIR without smuggling parser state

Structure earns its keep.

## TIR phases

One module AST build owns one `TemplateIrStore`. Parser emission writes text, expressions, child templates, slots, inserts, wrappers and control-flow roots directly into that store.

The phase sequence is:

[codeblock, $code("text"):
Parsed -> Composed -> Formatted -> Finalized
]

Teaching names for the parts:

- **slots** name holes that receive values or nested content
- **wrappers** wrap content in outer structure such as tags
- **control-flow edges** capture template-local `if` and loop structure before it becomes ordinary CFG in HIR

Exact view identity includes root, phase and value context. Consumers read through that authority rather than inventing parallel overlay stacks.

Folding requires `Composed` or later. AST-to-HIR handoff requires `Finalized`.

[diagram:
    [$insert("label"): TIR lives and dies inside AST]
    [$insert("caption"): Template structure gets a real home for exactly as long as the checker needs it, then leaves nothing behind for later stages to misread.]

    [stage:
        [node:
            [$insert("href"): ./]
            [$insert("eyebrow"): Built]
            [$insert("title"): Structure captured as TIR]
            Wrappers, slots, child values, control flow and placement order, kept as structure rather than flattened text.
        ]
    ]

    [stage:
        [node:
            [$insert("href"): ./]
            [$insert("eyebrow"): Classified]
            [$insert("title"): prepare_tir_view labels each piece]
            Foldable, runtime or helper. One owner decides, so finalisation never re-litigates it.
        ]

        [$insert("details"):
            [branch:
                [$insert("label"): Two exits]
                [fanout:
                [detail:
                    [$insert("href"): ../html-assembly-and-output/]
                    Static pieces fold to strings with insertion indexes
